---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Brief = `Streaming went up every year and CD sales went down every year.
Somebody wants to put "streaming killed the CD" in a
presentation. Check the data and tell them whether they can
say that.`;

const SampleOutput = `streams vs cds move the same way in 0 of 4 changes
streams vs cds move OPPOSITE in 4 of 4`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-2/cc-set-7" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back to Set 7
        </a>

        <h1>Code Challenge: Correlation Check</h1>

        <h4>
          Difficulty&nbsp;&nbsp;
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="brief">
          <h2>The Brief</h2>

          <Code code={Brief} frame="code" lang="txt" title="What they asked for" showLineNumbers={false} class="mt-3" />

          <p class="mt-4">
            <b>Write your requirements list before you write any code.</b> Input,
            calculate, output, and anything you had to decide for yourself. See{" "}
            <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-2/cc-set-7">Set 7</a> for what that looks like.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="notes">
          <h2>Notes</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>Write a procedure that compares two lists year by year and counts how often they move the <b>same</b> way and how often they move <b>opposite</b>.</li>
            <li>The answer here is a perfect opposite in every single year. <b>Do not stop there.</b></li>
            <li><b>The deliverable is a written verdict, not a number.</b> Say what the data supports, what it does not, and what you would need to collect to settle it.</li>
            <li>This one is more dangerous than the ice cream example at 2.18, because the plausible explanation might even be right. Say why that makes it harder, not easier.</li>
            <li>Name at least one other thing that changed over those same years and could be driving both.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="sample-output">
          <h2>Sample Output</h2>

          <Code code={SampleOutput} frame="terminal" title="Sample Output" lang="txt" showLineNumbers={false} class="mt-3" />

          <p class="mt-3">
            <b>Four out of four, and it still is not proof.</b> A correlation found in
            data does not necessarily indicate a causal relationship &mdash; and that
            holds even when the story sounds obviously true.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Your requirements list and your program file, named{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">cc-correlation-check</b>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
